## 5. Architectural Decision Matrix for Production Serving

The following matrix guides platform engineers in selecting the optimal memory optimization strategy based on workload characteristics:

| Workload Characteristic | Primary Bottleneck | Recommended Memory Optimization | Expected Latency & Throughput Impact |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **High Concurrency, Short Prompts** (e.g., Chatbot, Customer Support) | High request queuing & memory fragmentation | • PagedAttention<br>• FP8 KV-Cache | $3\times$–$4\times$ increase in max throughput; sub-15ms ITL |
| **Ultra-Long Document RAG** (e.g., Legal, Financial Analysis) | Prefill execution time & VRAM exhaustion | • Chunked Prefill<br>• FlashDecoding<br>• INT4-KV Quantization | P95 TTFT reduced by 60%; eliminates OOM errors |
| **Multi-Agent Swarms** (e.g., Shared Codebase Analysis) | Context duplication across agent instances | • RadixAttention Prefix Sharing<br>• Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA) | Up to 80% VRAM savings; 0ms prefill on shared context |
| **Edge / On-Device Serving** (e.g., Robotics, Mobile, Local PC) | Severely constrained physical RAM/VRAM | • AWQ / INT4 Model Weights<br>• StreamingLLM Attention Sinks | Model fits in <8GB memory; steady, deterministic latency |

