## 6. Conclusion

Optimizing memory usage and memory bandwidth in LLM inference is not merely an infrastructure cost-reduction measure; it is the fundamental architectural requirement for unlocking low-latency, long-context, and high-concurrency AI applications.

By integrating **hardware-aware quantization (FP8/INT4)**, **architectural compression (GQA/MLA)**, **virtualized memory paging (PagedAttention)**, **zero-copy prefix sharing (RadixAttention)**, and **sequence-parallel decoding (FlashDecoding)**, engineering teams can break through the memory wall—maximizing hardware utilization and delivering deterministic, single-digit millisecond latency across modern distributed backends.
